course: dictionary
lesson: 10782
title: A place in a myth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and names start with a capital letter. Valhalla is a name, so it has a big V. Context clues tell you what kind of thing it is: «Vikings believed in Odin, Thor with his hammer, Loki the trickster, and Valhalla, the hall of fallen warriors.» The words after the comma explain it for you.
explain: The sentence says Valhalla is a hall, a great building. Fallen here means warriors who died in battle, not people who tripped over. Swap in your meaning: Valhalla, the hall of dead warriors. Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
explain: Notice the words «Vikings believed». In the myth, Vikings believed that brave warriors chosen by the Valkyries feasted in Valhalla. Valhalla is not a real place you can visit, so we say what people believed. Stories, films and games use it often, and they can change the old myths, as «Marvel's Thor and Loki are very different from the old myths» shows.
fact: Valhalla is a name from Norse myth, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Valhalla is the great hall where the god Odin welcomed warriors who died bravely in battle.
fact: According to the myth, the Valkyries chose the brave warriors who went to Valhalla.
fact: Informally, valhalla can mean a wonderful place of honour, like «a Valhalla for football fans».
fact: Say «Vikings believed» when you talk about Valhalla, because it is a myth, not a real place.
exercise: «Vikings believed in Odin, Thor with his hammer, Loki the trickster, and Valhalla, the hall of fallen warriors.» What is Valhalla? | A kind of Viking ship | *A great hall in the old Norse myths, where Odin welcomed brave warriors | A real castle the Vikings lived in | The name of a Viking village
exercise: Find and copy one word that is a name with a capital letter. | the | battle | *Valhalla | warriors
exercise: Why do we write «Vikings believed» before saying Valhalla is a hall? | Because it is a word about football | Because Vikings wrote all the films | *Because it is a myth, not a real place | Because Valhalla was a real place in Norway
test: In the myth, who chose the brave warriors to go to Valhalla? | *The Valkyries | Thor with his hammer | Loki the trickster | Odin himself
test: What does valhalla mean informally? | A dangerous path in the hills | A type of Viking boat | A cold, dark cave | *A wonderful place of honour, like a heaven for some group
exam: Which sentence uses Valhalla correctly? | Valhalla was a fast red car in the film | *Vikings believed brave warriors feasted in Valhalla until the end of the world | My dog is named Valhalla and he is a terrier | Let's go to Valhalla for our holiday next summer
